# panel 214, lane land-214, 2026-10-14 (its provisional resolution; the
# compiler-engineer's shape x1).
#
# SYMPTOM: `int main(void);` in a header: clang's first error lies in the C this
# compiler writes for the program, at its own `int main(int argc, char
# **argv)`, the note in the header; told *internal error* at exit 2.
#
# FIX: R3: a first error in the program's C at a name of the compiler's own
# forms no group binds, its note in a group's header at that name, is the
# header's (`cli/own_names.hero`, `kept`).

extern "ffi-a-header-declaring-main-is-told.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function x1_f() -> i32

function main()
    print(x1_f())
